Bresenhams Line Drawing Algorithm
1. Accept the endpoints(x1,y1) and (x2,y2)
2. Calculate dx = x2-x1
dy=y2-y1
3. Initialize Starting Point x=x1, y=y1 plot(x,y)
4. Calculate e=2*dy-dx
5. i=1
6. while(e>=0)
{
y=y+1;
e=e-2*dx;
}
x=x+1;
e=e+2*dy
7. Plot(x,y)
8. i=i+1;
9. if(i<=dx) then go to step 6
10. Stop

Example :
Given: Start Point: (x1, y1) = (5, 5) End Point: (x2, y2) = (13, 9)
Step 1: Calculate dx and dy
dx = x2 − x1= 13 − 5= 8 dy = y2 − y1= 9 − 5= 4

